(meta (title "Folders are menus")
      (date 2026-09-22))

A folder's page is its @code{index.sz}, if it has one, and then a menu: a line
for each thing in the folder, with its title, a @code{/} after a folder's, and
its date on the right. A page's line says what its @code{(meta ...)} says, and
a folder's what its @code{index.sz} says. Anything else --- a picture, a text
file --- is listed by its name, and dated by when it was last written.

@section{The order}

Folders come first. The rest are newest first, unless the folder's
@code{index.sz} says otherwise:

@codeblock|{
(meta (title "Recipes") (sort title))     ; A to Z
(meta (sort date ascending))              ; oldest first
(meta (sort name descending))             ; by file name, Z to A
}|

@link["../recipes/"]{Recipes} is sorted by title, and
@link["../files/"]{Files} by name. This folder says nothing, and so is newest
first. A date that cannot be read as one, and so cannot be sorted by, comes
last.

@section{Hidden things}

A name that begins with @code{_} or @code{.} is left out of the menu, and no
URL reaches it: @link["../_drafts/unfinished.html"]{this draft} is not found.
The pieces of pages that others include are kept that way, in @code{_parts}.
@code{@"@"include} refuses a file that is not hidden, which would be a page of
its own as well.

@code{_resources} is the one hidden folder whose files are served, for the
site's style sheet and what it uses.

@include["../_parts/signature.sz"]
